  "before_interfaces": {
    "lem-common-submeasure-density-is-pointwise-minimum": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice (AC). Let $\\lambda$ be a sigma-finite positive\nmeasure on $(E,\\mathcal F)$, and let $\\rho$ and $\\sigma$ be finite positive\nmeasures absolutely continuous with respect to $\\lambda$. Suppose finite-valued\nnonnegative measurable functions $f,g:E\\to[0,\\infty)$ satisfy\n$$\\rho(A)=\\int_A f\\,d\\lambda,\\qquad \\sigma(A)=\\int_A g\\,d\\lambda\\qquad(A\\in\\mathcal F).$$\nThen\n$$\\eta(A):=\\int_A\\min\\{f,g\\}\\,d\\lambda$$\nis the greatest measure dominated by both $\\rho$ and $\\sigma$, where\ndomination means inequality on every measurable set."
    ],
    "lem-common-submeasure-and-bounded-radon-nikodym-density": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume the Axiom of Choice (AC). Let $\\rho$ and $\\sigma$ be finite positive\nmeasures on a measurable space $(E,\\mathcal F)$. Put $\\lambda=\\rho+\\sigma$.\nChoose nonnegative measurable Radon–Nikodym density representatives\n$f=d\\rho/d\\lambda$ and $g=d\\sigma/d\\lambda$, modified on a $\\lambda$-null set\nso that $f+g=1$ everywhere. Then\n$$\\eta(A):=\\int_A\\min\\{f,g\\}\\,d\\lambda\\qquad(A\\in\\mathcal F)$$\nis the greatest measure dominated by both $\\rho$ and $\\sigma$. The measurable\nfunction\n$$a:=\\begin{cases}\\min\\{1,g/f\\},&f>0,\\\\1,&f=0\\end{cases}$$\ntakes values in $[0,1]$ and is a version of $d\\eta/d\\rho$. Here $\\eta\\le\\rho$\nmeans $\\eta(A)\\le\\rho(A)$ for every $A\\in\\mathcal F$."
    ],
    "alg-metropolis-hastings-kernel": [
      "## Definition\n\nAssume AC. The **Metropolis–Hastings procedure** takes as input a standard-Borel\nspace $(\\mathsf X,\\mathcal X)$ ([[def-standard-borel-space]]), a target\nprobability measure $\\pi$ ([[def-probability-measure]]), and a probability\nkernel $Q$ from $(\\mathsf X,\\mathcal X)$ to itself\n([[def-measure-kernel-and-probability-kernel]]).\n\n1. On the product sigma-algebra ([[def-product-sigma-algebra-and-finite-product-sigma-algebras]]),\nform the proposal-flow measure $\\mu$ ([[def-measure]]) on\n$\\mathsf X\\times\\mathsf X$ by\n$$\\mu(C)=\\int_{\\mathsf X}Q(x,C_x)\\,\\pi(dx),\\qquad C_x=\\{y:(x,y)\\in C\\}.$$\nThis is a probability measure by [[lem-prior-and-model-kernel-define-joint-law]].\nLet $\\tau(x,y)=(y,x)$ and set $\\mu^{\\mathsf T}(C)=\\mu(\\tau^{-1}C)$.\n\n2. Set $\\eta=\\mu\\wedge\\mu^{\\mathsf T}$, the greatest measure dominated by both\nflows. Put $\\lambda_0=\\mu+\\mu^{\\mathsf T}$, which is a finite measure by\n[[thm-nonnegative-weighted-sums-of-measures]], and choose nonnegative measurable\nrepresentatives $f=d\\mu/d\\lambda_0$ and $g=d\\mu^{\\mathsf T}/d\\lambda_0$\nwith $f+g=1$ everywhere after modification on a $\\lambda_0$-null set. Define\n$$\\alpha(x,y)=\\begin{cases}\\min\\{1,g(x,y)/f(x,y)\\},&f(x,y)>0,\\\\1,&f(x,y)=0.\\end{cases}$$\nThis is a jointly measurable version of $d\\eta/d\\mu$ taking values in $[0,1]$.\n\n3. For $x\\in\\mathsf X$, compute the integrated acceptance probability\n$$a(x)=\\int_{\\mathsf X}\\alpha(x,y)\\,Q(x,dy)$$\nand rejection probability $r(x)=1-a(x)$.\n\n4. Return the transition rule\n$$P(x,A)=\\int_{\\mathsf X}\\mathbf1_A(y)\\alpha(x,y)\\,Q(x,dy)+\\mathbf1_A(x)r(x),\\qquad A\\in\\mathcal X.$$\nThe second term retains every rejected proposal as a self-transition.\n\nThe item [[lem-common-submeasure-and-bounded-radon-nikodym-density]] proves the\ncommon-submeasure construction and density-version claims in step 2."
    ],
    "lem-metropolis-hastings-density-ratio": [
      "## Statement\n\nAssume AC. Let $(\\mathsf X,\\mathcal X)$ be standard Borel\n([[def-standard-borel-space]]) and let $\\lambda$ be a sigma-finite positive\nmeasure ([[def-finite-sigma-finite-and-semifinite-measures]]) on it. Let the\ntarget probability have a finite-valued nonnegative measurable density\n$p:\\mathsf X\\to[0,\\infty)$, and suppose the proposal kernel has a finite-valued\nnonnegative jointly measurable density $q:\\mathsf X\\times\\mathsf X\\to[0,\\infty)$,\nso $\\pi(A)=\\int_Ap\\,d\\lambda$ and\n$Q(x,A)=\\int_Aq(x,y)\\,d\\lambda(y)$ for every $x$ and $A$. Let\n$\\mu(dx,dy)=\\pi(dx)Q(x,dy)$ be the forward proposal flow and let\n$\\mu^{\\mathsf T}$ be its transpose. Put\n$$m(x,y)=p(x)q(x,y),\\qquad m^{\\mathsf T}(x,y)=p(y)q(y,x).$$\nThere is a jointly measurable version $\\alpha_{\\rm cd}$ of\n$d(\\mu\\wedge\\mu^{\\mathsf T})/d\\mu$ given by\n$$\\alpha_{\\rm cd}(x,y)=\\begin{cases}\\min\\left\\{1,\\dfrac{p(y)q(y,x)}{p(x)q(x,y)}\\right\\},&m(x,y)>0,\\\\1,&m(x,y)=0.\\end{cases}$$\nThe version chosen by [[alg-metropolis-hastings-kernel]] agrees with this\ncommon-density version $\\mu$-almost everywhere; values on a forward-flow null\nset do not alter the accepted flow."
